GPIO_TC_001	GPIO Register Default Value Check	Verify all GPIO registers read back their expected default/reset values after system reset (hreset_n). Iterates through 49 register addresses and compares read data (masked with 0xFFFFFFFE) against default_value_array.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8	0x00	32	data_in	0	RO	0	hreset_n	System reset applied (hreset_n asserted then de-asserted). GPIO IP clock (ahb_clk) running. #define GPIO0 1 active.	1. Apply system reset (hreset_n=0 then hreset_n=1).
2. For each register address in addr_array[0..48], skip if skip_rst_array[i]==1.
3. Skip if read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 (not readable).
4. Read register at addr_array[i].
5. Mask read data with 0xFFFFFFFE.
6. Compare with default_value_array[i].	All 49 GPIO register addresses return their expected default values after reset. data_in=0, intr_raw_sts=0, intr_clr=0, pedge_intr_en=0, nedge_intr_en=0, level_sel=0, io_ctrl=1 (bit20), dout=0 (bit21). def_fail_cnt==0.	READ	Register Reset Value Verification	High	Not Executed	VRRW registers (offsets 0x80,0x94,0x98,0x9C,0xA0,0xA4,0xA8,0xAC,0xB0) are skipped via skip_rst_array. Bit0 masked off due to data_in being RO from external pin.
GPIO_TC_002	GPIO Register Write-Read Pattern 0xFFFFFFFF	Write 0xFFFFFFFF pattern to all writable GPIO registers and read back to verify write-read integrity. Write data is masked with write_mask_array before writing. Read data is masked with read_mask_array and compared against expected value.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1	0x00-0x90	32	pedge_intr_en, nedge_intr_en, level_sel, io_ctrl, dout	17-21	RW, RW2	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GPIO registers at default values. #define GPIO0 1 active.	1. Set data_wr = 0xFFFFFFFF.
2. For each register in addr_array, skip if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0.
3. Write (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) to register.
4. Read back each register, mask with read_mask_array[i].
5. Compute expected: (data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | (~write_mask & read_mask & default_value).
6. Compare read vs expected.	All writable fields read back 1s where write_mask allows. RO fields retain default values. wr_fail_cnt==0.	WRITE/READ	Register Write-Read Verification	High	Not Executed	VRRW registers skipped via skip_array. WO fields (intr_clr at bit16) not readable.
