GPIO_TC_008	GPIO Level Interrupt - Active High Level Selection (GPIO 8-39)	Verify GPIO level-sensitive interrupt generation with active-high level selection (level_sel=1). For each GPIO pin 8-39, configure input mode with level interrupt enabled at high level, trigger interrupt, verify raw status, group interrupt status, clear interrupt, and verify sysreg interrupt propagation.	test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8 (offset 0x00), gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (offset 0x84), gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (offset 0x88), LSS SYSREG RAW_STCR1	0x00, 0x84, 0x88	32	io_ctrl(bit20), level_sel(bit19), pedge_intr_en(bit17), intr_raw_sts(bit1), intr_clr(bit16)	0,1,16,17,19,20	RW, RW2, RO, WO	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GIC IRQ 87 enabled (for GPIO0). LSS SYSREG INTR_EN1 configured for GPIO0 interrupt. #define GPIO0 1 active.	1. Enable GIC IRQ 87 for GPIO0.
2. Write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 to enable GPIO0 interrupt at sysreg level.
3. For each GPIO i (0 to 31, representing GPIO_8 to GPIO_39):
   a. Write 0x00180000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) → sets io_ctrl=1 (input mode), level_sel=1 (active high), pedge_intr_en=1.
   b. Wait 50 cycles.
   c. Write (1<<i) to gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84) to enable group interrupt for this GPIO.
   d. Write 0xFFFFFFFF to SRAM (0xA0243FFC) to drive GPIO input high.
   e. Wait for interrupt (int_pend==0).
4. In ISR (Default_IRQHandler):
   a. Read gp0_gpio_8+(i*4), check bit1 (intr_raw_sts) is set.
   b. Read gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88), verify bit[i] is set.
   c. Write 0x00110000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) to clear interrupt (intr_clr=1).
   d. Read back register, verify value is 0x100001.
   e. Disable group interrupt (write 0 to 0x84).
   f. Verify group interrupt status cleared.
   g. Clear sysreg raw status and verify.
   h. Clear GIC IRQ 87.	For each GPIO pin 8-39: (1) intr_raw_sts (bit1) is set when input is high with level_sel=1. (2) Group interrupt status bit[i] in gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 is set. (3) After clearing, register reads 0x100001. (4) Group interrupt status returns to 0. (5) Sysreg interrupt cleared. test_err==0.	WRITE/READ/ISR	Interrupt Functional Verification	High	Not Executed	Tests all 32 GPIO pins (8-39) sequentially. Uses GIC IRQ 87 for GPIO0 instance. Verifies full interrupt chain: pin→raw_status→group_status→sysreg→GIC.
GPIO_TC_009	GPIO Level Interrupt - Active Low Level Selection (GPIO 8-39)	Verify GPIO level-sensitive interrupt generation with active-low level selection (level_sel=0). For each GPIO pin 8-39, configure input mode with level interrupt enabled at low level, trigger interrupt by driving pin low, verify raw status, group interrupt status, clear interrupt, and verify sysreg interrupt propagation.	test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8 (offset 0x00), gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (offset 0x84), gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (offset 0x88), LSS SYSREG RAW_STCR1	0x00, 0x84, 0x88	32	io_ctrl(bit20), level_sel(bit19), intr_raw_sts(bit1), intr_clr(bit16)	0,1,16,19,20	RW, RW2, RO, WO	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GIC IRQ 87 enabled. LSS SYSREG INTR_EN1 configured. Active-high level test (TC_008) completed.	1. For each GPIO i (0 to 31):
   a. Write 0x00100000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) → sets io_ctrl=1 (input mode), level_sel=0 (active low).
   b. Wait 50 cycles.
   c. Write (1<<i) to gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84).
   d. Write ~(1<<i) to SRAM (0xA0243FFC) to drive GPIO input low for pin i.
   e. Wait for interrupt.
2. In ISR: Same verification as TC_008.	For each GPIO pin 8-39: (1) intr_raw_sts is set when input is low with level_sel=0. (2) Group and sysreg interrupts propagate correctly. (3) Interrupt clearing works. test_err==0.	WRITE/READ/ISR	Interrupt Functional Verification	High	Not Executed	Complement of TC_008. Verifies active-low level detection. Uses inverted SRAM write pattern ~(1<<i) to drive specific pin low.
GPIO_TC_010	GPIO RO Field Verification - data_in Field	Verify that the data_in field (bit0) of each GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39) is read-only and reflects the current pin level regardless of input/output mode.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39	0x00-0x7C	32	data_in	0	RO	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GPIO pins at known state.	1. Read data_in (bit0) from each GPIO register.
2. Attempt to write 1 to bit0.
3. Read back and verify bit0 is unchanged (still reflects pin level).
4. Verify data_in reflects actual GPIO pin level.	data_in field is read-only. Write attempts do not modify bit0. Value reflects actual pin level.	READ	Read-Only Field Verification	Medium	Not Executed	data_in is sourced from gpio module. Bit0 masked in default check (0xFFFFFFFE mask).
GPIO_TC_011	GPIO WO Field Verification - intr_clr Field	Verify that the intr_clr field (bit16) of each GPIO register is write-only. Writing 1 clears the interrupt raw status. Writing 0 has no effect. Field is not readable.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39	0x00-0x7C	32	intr_clr	16	WO	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. Interrupt generated on GPIO pin.	1. Generate an interrupt on a GPIO pin (e.g., via level trigger).
2. Read register - verify intr_raw_sts (bit1) is set.
3. Write 1 to intr_clr (bit16).
4. Read register - verify intr_raw_sts (bit1) is cleared.
5. Write 0 to intr_clr (bit16) - verify no change.	Writing 1 to intr_clr clears the raw interrupt status. Writing 0 has no effect. intr_clr field reads as 0 (write-only).	WRITE	Write-Only Field Verification	Medium	Not Executed	WO field - write_mask includes bit16 but read_mask excludes it.
GPIO_TC_012	GPIO Interrupt Raw Status and Clear Register (gpio_intr_raw_stclr1) Verification	Verify the consolidated interrupt raw status and clear register at offset 0x80. Each bit corresponds to one GPIO pin (bit0=GPIO_8 through bit31=GPIO_39). Reading returns latched raw interrupt status. Writing 1 clears the corresponding interrupt.	test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en	program.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	gpio_intr_raw_stclr1	0x80	32	G8_intr_raw_stclr to G39_intr_raw_stclr	0-31	VRRW	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GPIO interrupts configured.	1. Configure GPIO pins for interrupt generation.
