GPIO_TC_018	GPIO Sysreg Interrupt Chain Verification	Verify the complete interrupt chain from GPIO pin through sysreg to GIC. Validates LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 gpio0_intr bit, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 enable, and GIC IRQ 87 for GPIO0 instance.	test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en	program.c	GPIO	GPIO0	1	LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1	LSS offsets 0x24, 0x28	32	gpio0_intr (bit1), gpio1_intr (bit2)	1, 2	RAWSTCR1, INTREN1	0	hreset_n	System reset completed. GIC initialized.	1. Enable GIC IRQ 87 (GPIO0) or 88 (GPIO1).
2. Write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 to enable gpio0_intr.
3. Trigger GPIO interrupt.
4. In ISR: Read LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, verify gpio0_intr bit set.
5. Write 1 to gpio0_intr bit in RAW_STCR1 to clear.
6. Read back, verify cleared.
7. Clear GIC IRQ.	Sysreg raw status reflects GPIO interrupt. Enable bit gates interrupt to GIC. Clearing raw status de-asserts interrupt. GIC IRQ correctly routed.	WRITE/READ/ISR	System-Level Interrupt Chain Verification	High	Not Executed	Cross-IP verification between GPIO and LSS SYSREG. Uses LSS_REGS spec for sysreg register mapping.